(I'm the primary developer of Tunnelblick, the OS X GUI for OpenVPN, having
taken over from Angelo Laub.)

Can someone make sure the release notes get updated when a release is made?

It's hard to decide whether/when to include a new version of OpenVPN into
Tunnelblick without knowing what is in the new version!

For example, the current download page at

http://openvpn.net/index.php/open-source/downloads.html

links to the release notes for 2.1.3 at

http://openvpn.net/index.php/open-source/documentation/change-log/71-21-cha=
nge-log.html

but the release notes do not describe the changes from 2.1.2 to 2.1.3. I
emailed openvpn-devel to find out, and David Sommerseth gave a very clear
reply, but I shouldn't keep posting to the entire the list to find out
what's in each release.

Thanks.

2010/11/5 Samuli Sepp=E4nen <samuli@...515...>

> Hi all,
>
> The next maintenance release of OpenVPN (2.1.4) will be released very
> soon, probably on Monday. This release will be the first one to be
> packaged for Debian and Ubuntu, the packages being already available for
> testing here:
>
> <http://build.openvpn.net/downloads/releases/ubuntu/10.04>
> <http://build.openvpn.net/downloads/releases/debian/5>
>
> I've smoke-tested the Ubuntu 10.04 i386 package myself and it seemed to
> work just fine. However, I'd love to know how these packages work for
> others (or if they don't) before publishing them "officially" on
> openvpn.net. So all feedback is most welcome!
>
> --
